<%# M11 admin alert (design card ⑦): what changed, why this admin is told, what to do if it wasn't expected %>
<p>Dear <%= @user.full_name %>,</p>

<p><strong><%= @headline %></strong> in <strong><%= @entity.name %></strong> on <%= l(@event.occurred_at) %>.</p>

<ul>
  <li>Done by: <%= @event.actor&.full_name || "an automatic job" %><%= " (signed in by CapHive support #{@event.impersonator.full_name})" if @event.impersonator && @event.impersonator_id != @event.actor_id %></li>
  <% if @event.ip_address.present? %><li>From the internet address: <%= @event.ip_address %></li><% end %>
</ul>

<p><strong>Why you got this:</strong> you are a company admin of <%= @entity.name %>. CapHive tells every company
admin when someone is given or loses the admin or approver role, when CapHive support access is switched on or off,
so a change nobody asked for is seen at once. (CapHive support signing in as one of your users, or switching into
your firm, shows in your notifications bell, not by email.) Every company admin gets this email, including the person who made the change.</p>

<p><strong>If you expected this,</strong> there is nothing to do.<br>
<strong>If you did not,</strong> open the person's user page and remove the role or switch support access off, then
write to support@caphive.com. The full history is on the Security Events page.</p>

<p><%= link_to "Open Security Events", security_events_url(host: "#{@entity.sub_domain}.#{ENV.fetch('DOMAIN', 'localhost')}"), class: "btn btn-outline-primary" %></p>

<p>Thank you,<br><%= @entity.name %> System</p>
